course: dictionary
lesson: 5547
title: Legless: two meanings, one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The context, meaning the words around the word, tells you which one the writer means. The word «legless» has two meanings: one is about bodies and animals, and one is slang.
explain: The first meaning is simple: having no legs. In science, a «legless lizard» is a lizard with no legs, and snakes are legless animals. When a text is about animals or body parts, legless means having no legs.
explain: The second meaning is British slang and is for grown-ups: «"Legless" is British slang for so drunk one cannot stand.» A story may use it to show an adult who drank far too much. This is a warning about alcohol, not something to copy.
fact: Legless means having no legs.
fact: A legless lizard is a lizard with no legs, and snakes are legless animals.
fact: In British slang, legless means so drunk that a person cannot stand or walk properly.
fact: The slang sense is for adults. Stories use it as a warning about drinking too much.
fact: A good check is to swap in the meaning. If "with no legs" fits the sentence, it is the first meaning; if it does not, the slang meaning is likely.
exercise: «The legless lizard slid across the warm sand.» What does legless mean here? | Very drunk | *Having no legs | Running very fast | Very tired from walking
exercise: In a science lesson about animals, what does legless mean? | *Having no legs, like a snake | Able to run very fast | Covered in mud | So drunk one cannot stand
exercise: Which word is slang for being drunk? | Refreshments | *Blotto | Lizard | Ancient
test: «A snake is a legless animal.» What does legless mean in this sentence? | Very old | *Having no legs | Very drunk | Very quick
test: Which is the slang meaning of legless? | Very old | *So drunk one cannot stand | Full of light | Having no legs
exam: Why might a story use legless for a grown-up who drank too much? | It means the grown-up was very happy | It is a cosy word for a drink | *It shows a warning about alcohol | Because it is the name of a lizard
